  <cac:ProcurementProject>
    <cbc:ID>EC-ENEST/SJJ/2025/EA-RP/0135</cbc:ID>
    <cbc:Name languageID="ENG">Technical Assistance for Climate Change Adaptation Planning and Improved Response</cbc:Name>
    <cbc:Description languageID="ENG">This project foresees implementation of activities focused on climate adaptation measures addressing both, river and torrential floods separately, taking into account their distinct characteristics and specificities, as outlined below:
River Floods
1.	Renewal of the Hydrological Information System (HIS) for the main sub-basins in Bosnia and Herzegovina, including flood events from 2010 to the present.
2.	Analysis of the impact of existing reservoirs on the water regime, with proposals for improving the management of high-water waves and enhancing water retention during dry periods.
3.	Development of guidelines for flood protection of agricultural land.
4.	Preparation of the manual “Living with Floods”, providing an overview of necessary measures and best practices for flood risk management.
Torrential Floods
1.	Development of a cadastre of torrential basins, including a sensitivity model based on existing erosion maps.
2.	Preparation of a study on increasing basin water retention capacity through measures aimed at reducing runoff and sediment transport, accompanied by a catalogue of applicable interventions.</cbc:Description>
    <cbc:ProcurementTypeCode listName="contract-nature">services</cbc:ProcurementTypeCode>
    <cbc:Note languageID="ENG">For any additional information, please refer to the document A5f "Additional information about the Contract Notice".
In case of unavailability or disruptions in the functioning of the electronic means of communication provided in Section 5.1.11 in the last 5 calendar days before the time limit for receipt indicated in Section 5.1.12, the contracting authority reserves the right to extend this time limit and publish the extension at the Internet address provided in Section 5.1.11, without a preceding publication of a corrigendum to this notice. Economic operators interested in this procurement are invited to subscribe to the call for tenders at the address in Section 5.1.11 in order to get notified when new information or documents are published.
</cbc:Note>
